            "target_entity_instance": "climate feedback parameter",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Linear climate feedback theory. The theory is based on the following equation described by Gregory et al. 11 N=F+a Tsurf where N is the change in global mean net TOA radiative imbalance (W m\u00af\u00b2), F is the effective forcing (Wm\u00af\u00b2), ATsurf is the global mean surface temperature change (\u00b0C), and a is the climate feedback parameter (Wm-2\u00b0C\u00af\u00b9). Thus, a can be obtained by regressing N as a function of time against ATsurf relative to a control climate. Here, the positive sign convention is used, meaning that a",
